return {h=12,w=655,cr=45,hc=20,bh=70,gr="medium",eg={"monster"},st={90,55,75,60,75,30},ab={{20,0},{12,0},{13,1}},genus={en="Licking Pokémon",es="Pokémon Lametazo",pt="Pokémon Lambedor"},flavor={en={[1]="Its tongue can be extended like a chameleon's. It leaves a tingling sensation when it licks enemies.",[2]="Its tongue can be extended like a chameleon's. It leaves a tingling sensation when it licks enemies.",[3]="Its tongue spans almost 7 feet and moves more freely than its forelegs. Its licks can cause paralysis.",[4]="Its tongue has well-developed nerves that run to the very tip, so it can be deftly manipulated.",[5]="Its long tongue, slathered with a gooey saliva, sticks to anything, so it is very useful.",[6]="It has a tongue that is over 6’6’’ long. It uses this long tongue to lick its body clean.",[7]="Whenever LICKITUNG comes across something new, it will unfailingly give it a lick. It does so because it memorizes things by texture and by taste. It is somewhat put off by sour things.",[8]="Whenever LICKITUNG comes across something new, it will unfailingly give it a lick. It does so because it memorizes things by texture and by taste. It is somewhat put off by sour things.",[9]="Whenever it sees something unfamiliar, it always licks the object because it memorizes things by texture and taste. It is somewhat put off by sour things.",[10]="Its tongue is twice the length of its body. It can be moved like an arm for grabbing food and attacking.",[11]="Its tongue can be extended like a chameleon’s. It leaves a tingling sensation when it licks enemies.",[12]="Instead of hands, it uses its tongue, which is twice its height. Its sticky saliva grips anything.",[13]="Instead of hands, it uses its tongue, which is twice its height. Its sticky saliva grips anything.",[14]="When it extends its over-six-foot-long tongue, its tail quivers. There is a possibility they are connected.",[15]="Its tongue has well-developed nerves that run to the very tip, so it can be deftly manipulated.",[16]="Its long tongue, slathered with a gooey saliva, sticks to anything, so it is very useful.",[17]="When it extends its over-six-foot-long tongue, its tail quivers. There is a possibility they are connected.",[18]="When it extends its over-six-foot-long tongue, its tail quivers. There is a possibility they are connected.",[21]="Being licked by its long, saliva-covered tongue leaves a tingling sensation. Extending its tongue retracts its tail.",[22]="Being licked by its long, saliva-covered tongue leaves a tingling sensation. Extending its tongue retracts its tail.",[23]="Its long tongue, slathered with a gooey saliva, sticks to anything, so it is very useful.",[24]="Its tongue is twice the length of its body. It can be moved like an arm for grabbing food and attacking.",[25]="Whenever Lickitung comes across something new, it will unfailingly give it a lick. It does so because it memorizes things by texture and by taste. It is somewhat put off by sour things.",[26]="Whenever Lickitung comes across something new, it will unfailingly give it a lick. It does so because it memorizes things by texture and by taste. It is somewhat put off by sour things.",[29]="It checks out whatever’s around it by licking everything. If you don’t clean off a spot where it’s licked you, you’ll break out in a rash!",[30]="It licks filth clean with its tongue. Whatever it licks always stinks afterward, so whether it’s really clean is...questionable.",[31]="Its tongue spans almost seven feet and moves more freely than its forelegs. Its licks can cause paralysis.",[32]="Its tongue spans almost seven feet and moves more freely than its forelegs. Its licks can cause paralysis.",[33]="If this Pokémon’s sticky saliva gets on you and you don’t clean it off, an intense itch will set in. The itch won’t go away, either.",[34]="Bug Pokémon are Lickitung’s main food source. This Pokémon paralyzes its prey with a lick from its long tongue, then swallows the prey whole.",[39]="Wields its long tongue deftly, as though it were an arm. The Pokémon's viscous saliva, once it has been collected and boiled down, yields a strong and highly useful adhesive."},es={[23]="Su larga lengua, recubierta de saliva pegajosa, se pega a todo, por lo que es muy útil.",[24]="La lengua es tan larga que duplica su altura. Es útil porque puede moverla para agarrar comida y atacar.",[25]="Cada vez que Lickitung se encuentra con algo que no conoce, le da un lametazo. Es la forma que tiene de memorizar las cosas, por la textura y el sabor. No soporta los sabores ácidos.",[26]="Cada vez que Lickitung se encuentra con algo que no conoce, le da un lametazo. Es la forma que tiene de memorizar las cosas, por la textura y el sabor. No soporta los sabores ácidos.",[29]="Identifica las cosas lamiéndolas con su larga lengua. Hay que tener cuidado, pues si no se tratan, sus lametones tienen efectos urticantes.",[30]="Se limpia y acicala a base de lengüetazos, aunque el olor que deja su saliva sugiere de todo menos pulcritud.",[31]="Su lengua puede llegar a medir dos metros y la mueve con más soltura que las patas delanteras. Sus lametazos pueden causar parálisis.",[32]="Su lengua puede llegar a medir dos metros y la mueve con más soltura que las patas delanteras. Sus lametazos pueden causar parálisis.",[33]="Si sus lametones no se tratan a tiempo, su saliva pegajosa y urticante puede provocar picores persistentes.",[34]="Se nutre principalmente de Pokémon insecto, a los que paraliza primero lamiéndolos con su larga lengua y luego engulle de un bocado."},pt="Maneja a língua comprida com habilidade, como se fosse um braço. A saliva viscosa deste Pokémon, depois de coletada e fervida, rende uma cola forte e muito útil."},evo={{s=108},{s=463,from=108,c={{t="level-up",move=205}}}},moves={[1]={1,35,1,48,7,23,15,50,23,111,31,21,39,103},[2]={1,35,1,48,7,23,15,50,23,111,31,21,39,103},[3]={1,122,7,48,13,111,19,23,25,35,31,50,37,21,43,103},[4]={1,122,7,48,13,111,19,23,25,35,31,50,37,21,43,103},[5]={1,